  m_Script: {fileID: 11500000, guid: 3ff6acaa8b9f1994499dd387e6188532, type: 3}
  m_Name: 
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: 
  Comments: 
  Warning: 'Please be aware that when post processing is applied as a second pass
    (for fulldome and VR renders) that no depth or motion vectors are available and
    the process is applied only to a 2D image of the first render pass. This means
    that motion blur and depth of field cannot be applied for these types of renders.
    However, when rendering standard cameras with post processing enabled, any fitlers
    may be used.


    Applying Motion Blur in Post

    If motion blur is desired,
    there are 3rd party applications such as Adobe After Effects which can generate
    decent motion blur from a video or image sequence. You can also render at a higher
    frame rate and use frame blending. '
